Apple today released HomePod software version 27.2.1, but it <a href="https://x.com/itspdfu/status/2121330608358240454">does not enable Siri AI on the HomePod mini 2</a>. Apple's website continues to say the feature is "coming in a future software update," but it has not provided a timeframe.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/homepod-mini-2-feature2.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1070600" /><br/>
Due to the HomePod mini 2 having <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/04/homepod-mini-2-ram/">only 2GB of RAM</a>, well below the minimum 8GB of RAM required for dedicated Siri AI, personal context requests will require a paired Apple Intelligence–enabled iPhone or iPad with Siri AI turned on. <br/>
<br/>
<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/13/apple-releases-tvos-27-2-1/">tvOS 27.2.1 was also released today</a>, and it enables Siri AI on the Apple TV 4K (2nd generation) and Apple TV 4K (3rd generation). Siri AI is an opt-in feature on these devices, so after installing the update you will need to open the Settings app and tap on General → Siri → Siri AI (Beta). This will initiate a download with support.<br/>
<br/>
